on-with-russia/a-79649641--99619951a602.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-warn-of-espionage-risks-as-slovakia-restores-military-diplomatic-representation-with-russia/a-79649641?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovakia is restoring military-diplomatic relations with Russia for the first time since 2022. The government has defended the move but critics warn of espionage risks and further damage to trust within NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbf732bfdd9c14c40454ad9c80b3962bb4a814db1e03ad9a83044da67d66a169</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>What is holding back Cyprus's Schengen ambitions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aea27aee6e18994360c53b0f3343fce84692dbe03966c69252e4ee3e9b6f29cf</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488--5f69812ab764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-is-holding-back-cyprus-s-schengen-ambitions/a-79641488?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission says Cyprus is ready to join the Schengen Area. Yet questions relating to the island's division and British military bases could still complicate its path to Europe's border-free travel zone.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Starlink India launch: Why Elon Musk is still waiting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d72aae000f80aa1c4284ec3afddc20a2b08e0e031edad88cb08fd48669817213</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043--4f745799dbba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/starlink-india-launch-why-elon-musk-is-still-waiting/a-79643043?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite securing key approvals, the Starlink satellite internet service remains in regulatory limbo, raising questions about security clearances, competition and India’s investment climate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Iran 'highly likely' to be behind RAF Fairford incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14357fb5e6eb69148e64828b222633a5d0f370cb22f9194055bef0525763a039</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941--7cd1b910595f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-iran-highly-likely-to-be-behind-raf-fairford-incident/a-79645941?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament there were "strong indications" of Iranian involvement. The government summoned Iran's ambassador. The scare at RAF Fairford led to the withdrawal of USAF B-1 heavy bombers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reports arrests of 2 Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with Starlink station fire last month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad5b131fc1429234b62f697ddd0a7d37e62cece14bd06ea307438c95472f9f9a</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-las/a-79646138--0f2bfafb19a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reports-arrests-of-2-turkish-citizens-in-germany-in-connection-with-starlink-station-fire-last-month/a-79646138?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have reported the arrests of two Turkish citizens in Germany in connection with alleged sabotage of a Starlink station last month. Prime Minister Donald Tusk called the fire an act of "hybrid warfare."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Viral videos falsely linked to Riyadh airport attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c5fb349e22edc7ec280ff9696b37fc461034b5fea092d195252e64d961dae7c</id><updated>2026-10-14T05:04:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037--a62cb3e36a4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-viral-videos-falsely-linked-to-riyadh-airport-attacks/a-79643037?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many videos claiming to show an attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport have gone viral online. DW Fact check analyzes some of the most-shared footage and finds evidence it was created using AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
